Mix: a hook of beam.com after the start of Mix

beam.com has a git client of its own (beam_com_git_scm, a source of
Mix). The Mix build of beam.com ("beam.com DIR -o FILE") adds it to the
sources of Mix when PATH has no git program. A user who runs Mix itself
("beam.com mix deps.get", "beam.com mix compile") got Mix.SCM.Git, which
stops with :enoent with no git program.

After the start of the supervisor of Mix, call :beam_com_mix.started/0
when it is exported. beam.com loads that module at the start of each
tool of Elixir. A usual install of Elixir has no such module, so nothing
changes there.

--- a/lib/mix/lib/mix.ex
+++ b/lib/mix/lib/mix.ex
@@ -463,7 +463,19 @@
     Mix.Local.append_paths()
     children = [Mix.Sync.PubSub, Mix.State, Mix.TasksServer, Mix.ProjectStack]
     opts = [strategy: :one_for_one, name: Mix.Supervisor, max_restarts: 0]
-    Supervisor.start_link(children, opts)
+
+    with {:ok, _} = ok <- Supervisor.start_link(children, opts) do
+      # A hook of beam.com (one file with OTP and Elixir): after the start
+      # of Mix, :beam_com_mix.started/0 adds the git client of the file
+      # to the sources of Mix when PATH has no git. A usual install has
+      # no module :beam_com_mix, and the module is not loaded in a plain
+      # run of this Mix.
+      if function_exported?(:beam_com_mix, :started, 0) do
+        :beam_com_mix.started()
+      end
+
+      ok
+    end
   end
 
   @impl true
